  private static let warmTranscriptCacheLimit = 16
  /// Upper bound for mounting a COMPLETE cached transcript during the push when only the
  /// disk heights are warm and the in-memory parse cache is cold (see the seed's coverage
  /// gate). Keeps a pathological transcript from turning the push into a long parse.
  // `coldFullWindowMountLimit` (400) is gone with the windowed seed. It capped four
  // separate full-window conditions that no longer exist; the seed mounts the cached
  // transcript whole, matching the core's unbounded window.
  private struct WarmTranscriptSnapshot {
    let rows: [ChatListRow]
    let sourceRows: [[String: Any]]
    let liveHeightStore: [String: RowHeightCacheEntry]
  }
  private static var warmTranscriptSnapshots: [String: WarmTranscriptSnapshot] = [:]
  private static var warmTranscriptSnapshotOrder: [String] = []
  /// Disk-persisted exact row heights (survive relaunch, unlike the warm snapshots
  /// above). Keyed by row key; validated against the row's content signature, width,
  /// and expand state before use, then promoted into the in-memory caches. This is
  /// what lets a cold reopen mount with exact sizing instead of estimated heights
  /// that the progressive warmup later corrects with visible offset nudges.
  private struct PersistedHeightEntry: Codable {
    let w: Double
    let s: String
    let h: Double
    let v: String
    let sig: String
    /// Per-field short hashes of the content signature (every row), so a `reason=sig`
    /// miss can diff element-wise and NAME the field that flipped between
    /// measure-time and reopen instead of guessing. Optional → old on-disk entries
    /// decode fine.
    let f: [String]?
    /// The height was a guess when it was measured (square media fallback, thumb-derived
    /// aspect, unresolved reply chip). Optional → old on-disk entries decode fine.
    let p: Bool?
  }
  /// Bump on ANY change to bubble layout math (paddings, meta placement, RTL rules,
  /// grouped-name reserves, …). Persisted heights measured under a different revision
  /// describe cells that no longer exist; content signatures cannot catch that (the
  /// rows never changed), and trusting them renders bubbles taller or shorter than
  /// their cells — the overlapping-RTL-bubbles bug. Restore discards mismatched files
  /// wholesale; the next open re-measures fresh behind the reopen raster.
  // r4: r3 was written to disk by a build where RTL bubbles used the INLINE layout. That
  // layout was reverted (RTL stacks its meta again), so every persisted r3 RTL height is
  // one meta-row too short — the cell comes back shorter than the bubble it renders and the
  // bubbles overlap. A revision is only reusable while the geometry that produced it is
  // still the geometry in force; reverting a layout needs a NEW revision, not the old one.
  // Bumped when agent-turn height floor / width rule changes so disk heights re-measure.
  // r6: documents got their own cell (a file row + page preview inside the bubble) where
  // they used to render as a plain text bubble or an image, and the live agent plate is
  // now quantised. Every r5 height for those rows describes a bubble that no longer
  // exists, and this is exactly the case content signatures cannot see — the rows never
  // changed, so `auditSeedTrustedHeights` validates the stale height and it sticks. That
  // is what painted an event caption and its timestamp BELOW the plate: the slot was
  // sized for the old bubble, the cell clamped the plate to the slot, and the caption
  // (placed from the full metrics) landed outside it.
  // r8 is not a layout-math change: every file written before it can contain SQUARE-FALLBACK
  // media heights, which the seed then trusts on a width match alone. There is no way to tell
  // a poisoned entry from a good one after the fact (the row's content signature is identical
  // either way), so the whole generation is discarded once and rebuilt from real measurements.
  // r9: the timestamp now rides the reaction strip row instead of the plate bottom, and
  // the strip reserves its width — every r8 height for a reacted row is the old geometry.
  // r11: RTL reactions share the meta row; video-note expand is a scale, not a height-morph.
  private static let bubbleLayoutRevision = "r11-videonote-scale"
  private struct PersistedHeightsFile: Codable {
    let rev: String
    let e: [String: PersistedHeightEntry]
  }
  private var persistedHeightsByKey: [String: PersistedHeightEntry] = [:]
  /// Trust-then-verify seed sizing. During the presentation seed's mount, a persisted
  /// height is promoted on a WIDTH match alone — a dictionary lookup — instead of
  /// validating the ~50-field content signature per row (String(describing:) over
  /// large agent payloads; measured as the posMs≈215 bulk of the mount, which is why
  /// the transcript kept landing AFTER the push animation instead of during it).
  /// Signatures still gate correctness: `auditSeedTrustedHeights` re-checks every
  /// trusted key OFF-MAIN after the push settles and reloads only rows whose content
  /// actually changed since their height was persisted — which is almost always none.
  private var seedTrustsPersistedHeights = false
  /// Keys promoted on trust during the current seed, with the state signature and
  /// content version captured at promote time (both are main-thread-derived, so the
  /// off-main audit compares captured values instead of recomputing them).
  private var seedTrustedHeightKeys: [String: (state: String, contentVersion: String)] = [:]
  /// Keys a cell has already reported as too short for the bubble it renders, so the
